@@ -433,6 +488,7 @@
     "Both profiles share the original root-domain lifecycle and runqueue membership operations. The native archive also builds unmodified CPU priority and deadline management. The original realtime bandwidth defaults and deadline bandwidth initialization have one owner in sched_ratio.c.",
     "The regular scheduler keeps fair.c runtime accounting. Native class callbacks consume the increment of the retained Runtime sample. The native publication owns the execution total and system time. The Linux runqueue clock owns exec_start.",
     "The original fair, RT and deadline queue constructors are shared by the regular scheduler and the native Initial task.",
+    "The native archive builds the kernel-thread branch of original fork.c and keeps its resource constructors and unwind. Native copy_process uses the existing stack, admission, dormant publication, and activation hooks. The regular kernel retains its user process and memory-management paths.",
     "This manifest records source provenance only; it does not establish compilation, linking, execution or native admission."
   ]
